      "status": "RESOLVED_REACHABLE_HORIZONTAL_CONTINUATION",
      "reason": "0039 records A/B/C/D at scrollLeft=0 within reachable horizontal ranges 0..54, 0..54, 0..68 and 0..286. The existing delivered option-body CSS uses overflow-x:auto. Complementary actual pixel observations settle the previously unseen marks: A's opening parenthesis, first x_1 q^5 and middle terms are recorded in 0054, and 0060 at A=52/54 explicitly records its final x_1q^(2k+1), complete raised 2k+1, plus sign, subscript 1 and closing parenthesis. B's opening and terms through x_1q^(m+1) are explicitly recorded in 0057; 0066 at B=52/54 explicitly records x_1q^(2k) followed by a complete closing parenthesis and legible overlapping middle terms. C's opening and powers 8, 40, 298, 2m-2 and 2m+2 are explicitly recorded in 0065; 0073 at C=66/68 explicitly records its complete final x_1 q^{4k} and immediately following closing parenthesis. D's opening and first three additive terms are recorded in 0065 and 0073. Its overlapping continuation is explicitly recorded through x_1+(m-1)q in 0078, the following comma and next x in 0080, next x_1 in 0081, and x_1+(m+1)q in 0088. 0089 records the next comma; 0096 at D=284/286 explicitly records the final x_1+2kq and complete outer closing parenthesis, as well as both inner closing parentheses after m-1 and m+1. These joined recorded observations account for the actual missing terms, signs, powers and closing delimiters; no single partial frame is promoted to whole-option approval, and no glyph is inferred from DOM targets or a saved maximum. All cited complementary observations are in actual completed-and-closed DISPLAY_PASS bindings from the assigned 0054..0096 native sequence. No image was opened by this technical reviewer.",
